  "en": {
    "kind": "Song cycle",
    "about": [
      "The songs were written in 1966 for a performance at the Lycabettus Theatre planned for March 1967, cancelled by the coup. They were recorded in October–November 1970, under the junta, with Nikos Xylouris as “Psaronikos” and a twelve-piece orchestra.",
      "It is regarded as an emblematic work of the “return to roots” movement, combining Pontic and Cretan lyras, clarinet, flute, Cretan lute and cello."
    ]
